Loon-specific transport, policy and diagnostics are separate Apache-2.0 code.
Lab work by aijc123 includes bounded admission, balanced existing-traffic trials,
local transfer statistics, DNS diagnostics and existing-response SIDX observation.
The 0.1.14 automatic profile adds one-switch operation, conservative size/load/error
scheduling, bounded recent events and marked request-version summaries. BTR's regional
host facts and successful-node preference inform the separately implemented Loon policy;
its browser streaming/progress/buffer controller is not claimed as a Loon capability.
The isolated 0.1.15 candidate adds completion-only gain/tail evaluation,
bounded adjacent-rung trials and regression recovery, reusing the existing local
balanced comparator. BTR's trial/backoff/rest principles inform this separate
Apache-2.0 Loon implementation; its player-only signals are not fabricated.
The design also references nishuodedui1145-del/PiliPlus and MyTVB-Speed-Boost;
their source is not copied. See RANGE-EXPERIMENT.md for details and limits.

Optional gateway work by aijc123 adds private-LAN Loon request rewriting,
persistent validated streaming, cancellation, process budgets and diagnostics.
BTR cdn-resolver.js and idm-downloader.js are preserved unchanged under MIT
at the same fixed commit; only the reviewed Semaphore portion is loaded from
the downloader. Hashes and sources are in gateway-provenance.json.
